.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1036 AM PDT Sat Sep 12 2026

VFR across the region with low confidence that stratus will return
tonight. Guidance is showing a largely drier airmass moving in
tonight which is decreasing confidence that we will see widespread
stratus coverage. More favorable conditions for localized
fog/stratus development exist along the coast where buoys are
showing an upwards transfer of heat/moisture from the sea to the
air (SST are warmer than air temperatures above the buoy). Expect
gusty winds today with widespread gusts between 25 to 35 knots.
Locally stronger gusts are possible in areas where terrain
promotes wind funneling.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the TAF period. Gusty onshore winds
are expected today with gusts between 25 to 35 knots forecasted
this afternoon into the evening. Winds decrease slightly overnight
but strengthen again by Sunday morning. The SFO-WMC gradient peaks
around +13 mb today which correlates to strong onshore winds.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO. Strong onshore winds are
expected this afternoon/evening with gusts to around 35 knots
possible.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Low confidence that stratus will
return tonight but if it does return it likely will not be until
after 12Z. Given the low confidence, have only included a tempo
for tonight`s stratus coverage after 12Z. Gusty onshore winds
peaking around 25 knots are expected today before diminishing
overnight. Breezier conditions are expected again tomorrow but
winds should be weaker than those observed today.

